## Film and page media

Everything under site/ (the landing page, the Afterparty film, its captions, posters, icons and fonts) is part of this
project. Unless a line below says otherwise it is licensed under the MIT License above.

- Film picture. The animated film is rendered from original code (Remotion, React, SVG and three.js) by Dror Lazar. The
  characters ("Bloops"), props, interface scenes and end card are original artwork. The painted backgrounds and props
  (desk, office wall, circuit board, keyboard, calendar and similar) were generated with OpenAI GPT Image 2.5 from text
  directions by Dror Lazar and split into layers; use of those images is subject to OpenAI's terms for generated output.
  The app screens in the film are recordings of this project's own interface on a sample folder.
- Film voice. The narration is synthetic speech generated with ElevenLabs (Eleven v3, the library voice "Jessica") from
  Dror Lazar's own script. It is subject to the ElevenLabs terms in force when it was generated.
- Film music. The score is instrumental music generated with ElevenLabs Music (v2.5, through fal.ai) from text style
  descriptions. It contains no vocals and no sampled or stock music.
- Film sound effects. Short sound effects come from recordings placed in the public domain (CC0 1.0): Freesound
  contributors (https://freesound.org) and Kenney (https://kenney.nl).
- Captions (afterparty.vtt) and chapter data are original text under the MIT License.
- Posters, social image and icons. Stills are frames of the film. The app icon, favicons and touch icons are original
